Duke Nukem 3D (apps/duke3d)

Engine (engine/)
  EDuke32, by Richard "TerminX" Gobeille, Evan Ramos and contributors,
  based on the Duke Nukem 3D source code by 3D Realms (released 2003) and
  the Build engine by Ken Silverman.
  https://voidpoint.io/terminx/eduke32, commit
  ec5824db81817866f70da326d3811bb0f52b3517 (master, 2026-08-07).
  Licenses:
    Duke Nukem 3D's game code and EDuke32's own code: GNU General Public
    License, version 2 (engine/gpl-2.0.txt).
    The Build engine: Ken Silverman's BUILD license (engine/BUILDLIC.TXT),
    which allows free distribution only, over the internet, never for
    money. This app is free and frunk.store charges nothing for it.

